![critical](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/critical.svg)

`BlockingTask::new` uses a hardcoded `TaskId`, which will cause collisions. `BlockingTask::new` should accept a `TaskId` to ensure each task has a unique identifier.

```suggestion
    fn new(func: F, task_id: TaskId) -> Self {
        Self {
            func: Some(func),
            context: TaskContext::new(task_id).with_priority(Priority::Normal),
            _phantom: std::marker::PhantomData,
        }
    }
