_⚠️ Potential issue_

**同様のコンソールエラー監視の問題が存在します**

前のテストと同じ問題があります。エラーリスナーの設定が遅すぎるため、実際のエラーを捕捉できません。



同様の修正を適用してください：

```diff
+      // エラーを監視するためのリスナーを事前に設定
+      const consoleErrors = [];
+      page.on('console', msg => {
+        if (msg.type() === 'error' && !msg.text().includes('Key input error')) {
+          consoleErrors.push(msg.text());
+        }
+      });
+      
       // 無効なキーを押す
       const invalidKeys = ['q', 'w', 'e', 't', 'y', 'u', 'i', 'o'];

       for (const key of invalidKeys) {
         await page.keyboard.press(key);
         await page.waitForTimeout(100);
       }

-      // エラーが発生しないことを確認
-      const consoleErrors = [];
-      page.on('console', msg => {
-        if (msg.type() === 'error' && !msg.text().includes('Key input error')) {
-          consoleErrors.push(msg.text());
-        }
-      });
-      
       expect(consoleErrors.length).toBe(0);
```

<!-- suggestion_start -->

<details>
<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>

> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**
> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.

```suggestion
      // エラーを監視するためのリスナーを事前に設定
      const consoleErrors = [];
      page.on('console', msg => {
        if (msg.type() === 'error' && !msg.text().includes('Key input error')) {
          consoleErrors.push(msg.text());
        }
      });

      // 無効なキーを押す
      const invalidKeys = ['q', 'w', 'e', 't', 'y', 'u', 'i', 'o'];

      for (const key of invalidKeys) {
        await page.keyboard.press(key);
        await page.waitForTimeout(100);
      }

      expect(consoleErrors.length).toBe(0);
```

</details>

<!-- suggestion_end -->

<details>
<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>

```
In tests/e2e/ui-controls.spec.js around lines 207 to 214, the console error
listener is set up too late, causing some errors to be missed. Move the
page.on('console') event listener setup to an earlier point before any actions
that might trigger console errors. This ensures all relevant console errors are
captured in the consoleErrors array before the expect assertion runs.
```

</details>

<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:panther -->

<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->

![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

The dependency array `[selectedVoice]` for this `useEffect` is likely not what you want, as it will cause the effect to re-run every time a voice is selected. This effect's purpose is to load the list of available voices and set an initial default, so it should only run once when the component mounts. Consider using an empty dependency array `[]`.

```
  }, []);
```

